   166|        <div class="highlight-box">
   167|            <strong>💡 Key Takeaway:</strong> Cancer treatment in China costs 60-80% less than in the US and Europe, with world-class oncology centers offering advanced treatments including immunotherapy, targeted therapy, and proton therapy.
   168|        </div>
   169|
   170|        <h2>Why Choose China for Cancer Treatment?</h2>
   171|        
   172|        <p>China has emerged as a leading destination for international cancer patients seeking high-quality, affordable oncology care. With <strong>5 of the world's top 10 cancer hospitals</strong> (according to Nature Index), China offers:</p>
   173|
   174|        <ul>
   175|            <li><strong>Significant Cost Savings:</strong> 60-80% lower than US/European prices</li>
   176|            <li><strong>Advanced Technology:</strong> Latest immunotherapy, CAR-T cell therapy, and proton therapy</li>
   177|            <li><strong>Experienced Specialists:</strong> High patient volumes mean extensive experience</li>
   178|            <li><strong>Shorter Wait Times:</strong> Treatment can begin within days, not months</li>
   179|            <li><strong>Integrated Care:</strong> Traditional Chinese Medicine combined with Western oncology</li>
   180|        </ul>
   181|
   182|        <h2>Cancer Treatment Cost Comparison</h2>
   183|
   184|        <p>The following table shows typical costs for common cancer treatments in China compared to the United States:</p>
   185|
   186|        <table class="cost-table">
   187|            <thead>
   188|                <tr>
   189|                    <th>Treatment Type</th>
   190|                    <th>USA Cost</th>
   191|                    <th>China Cost</th>
   192|                    <th>Your Savings</th>
   193|                </tr>
   194|            </thead>
   195|            <tbody>
   196|                <tr>
   197|                    <td>Breast Cancer Surgery</td>
   198|                    <td>$50,000-80,000</td>
   199|                    <td>$8,000-15,000</td>
   200|                    <td class="savings">70-80%</td>
   201|                </tr>
   202|                <tr>
   203|                    <td>Lung Cancer Treatment (Full Course)</td>
   204|                    <td>$150,000-250,000</td>
   205|                    <td>$30,000-60,000</td>
   206|                    <td class="savings">75-80%</td>
   207|                </tr>
   208|                <tr>
   209|                    <td>Colorectal Cancer Surgery</td>
   210|                    <td>$60,000-100,000</td>
   211|                    <td>$12,000-20,000</td>
   212|                    <td class="savings">75-80%</td>
   213|                </tr>
   214|                <tr>
   215|                    <td>Immunotherapy (PD-1/PD-L1)</td>
   216|                    <td>$150,000/year</td>
   217|                    <td>$15,000-25,000/year</td>
   218|                    <td class="savings">80-85%</td>
   219|                </tr>
   220|                <tr>
   221|                    <td>CAR-T Cell Therapy</td>
   222|                    <td>$475,000</td>
   223|                    <td>$120,000-150,000</td>
   224|                    <td class="savings">70%</td>
   225|                </tr>
   226|                <tr>
   227|                    <td>Proton Therapy</td>
   228|                    <td>$150,000</td>
   229|                    <td>$40,000-60,000</td>
   230|                    <td class="savings">60-70%</td>
   231|                </tr>
   232|                <tr>
   233|                    <td>Radiation Therapy (Full Course)</td>
   234|                    <td>$50,000-80,000</td>
   235|                    <td>$10,000-18,000</td>
   236|                    <td class="savings">75-80%</td>
   237|                </tr>
   238|                <tr>
   239|                    <td>Chemotherapy (Per Cycle)</td>
   240|                    <td>$10,000-30,000</td>
   241|                    <td>$1,500-4,000</td>
   242|                    <td class="savings">80-85%</td>
   243|                </tr>
   244|            </tbody>
   245|        </table>
