   270|        <h2>What's Included in the Cost?</h2>
   271|
   272|        <p>When you receive a treatment quote from Chinese hospitals, it typically includes:</p>
   273|
   274|        <ul>
   275|            <li><strong>Initial Consultation:</strong> $50-150 (vs $300-500 in US)</li>
   276|            <li><strong>Diagnostic Tests:</strong> CT, MRI, PET-CT, biopsies</li>
   277|            <li><strong>Treatment:</strong> Surgery, chemotherapy, radiation, or targeted therapy</li>
   278|            <li><strong>Hospital Stay:</strong> Private rooms available</li>
   279|            <li><strong>Post-Treatment Care:</strong> Follow-up consultations</li>
   280|            <li><strong>Medical Translation:</strong> English-speaking coordinators</li>
   281|        </ul>
   282|
   283|        <p><strong>Not included:</strong> Travel, accommodation, meals, and companion expenses.</p>
   284|
   285|        <h2>Advanced Treatments Available</h2>
   286|
   287|        <h3>🧬 Immunotherapy (PD-1/PD-L1 Inhibitors)</h3>
   288|        <p>China is a global leader in immunotherapy, with domestically produced PD-1 inhibitors costing 80% less than imported versions while maintaining equivalent efficacy. Drugs like sintilimab, toripalimab, and camrelizumab are widely available.</p>
   289|
   290|        <h3>🧪 CAR-T Cell Therapy</h3>
   291|        <p>China has approved multiple CAR-T therapies for blood cancers at approximately 30% of US costs. Several hospitals have extensive experience with this cutting-edge treatment.</p>
   292|
   293|        <h3>⚛️ Proton Therapy</h3>
   294|        <p>Multiple centers in Shanghai and Beijing offer proton therapy for precise tumor targeting with reduced side effects.</p>
   295|
   296|        <h3>🎯 Targeted Therapy</h3>
   297|        <p>Genetic testing and personalized targeted therapies are standard practice at top Chinese cancer centers.</p>
   298|
   299|        <h2>Patient Success Stories</h2>
   300|
   301|        <div class="highlight-box">
   302|            <p><strong>Sarah M., USA:</strong> "I was quoted $180,000 for lung cancer treatment in the US. In Beijing, I received the same immunotherapy protocol for $35,000. The care was excellent, and I'm now in remission."</p>
   303|        </div>
   304|
   305|        <div class="highlight-box">
   306|            <p><strong>Robert K., Canada:</strong> "The wait time for cancer surgery in Canada was 4 months. In Shanghai, I had surgery within 10 days of arrival. The total cost, including travel, was still 60% less than Canadian private options."</p>
   307|        </div>
   308|
   309|        <h2>How to Get Started</h2>
   310|
   311|        <ol>
   312|            <li><strong>Submit Your Medical Records:</strong> Send your diagnosis, imaging, and pathology reports</li>
   313|            <li><strong>Receive Treatment Plan:</strong> Get a detailed proposal within 48-72 hours</li>
   314|            <li><strong>Apply for Medical Visa:</strong> We provide invitation letters for M visa</li>
   315|            <li><strong>Travel Arrangements:</strong> Airport pickup and hospital coordination</li>
   316|            <li><strong>Begin Treatment:</strong> Start your care journey with dedicated support</li>
   317|        </ol>
   318|
   319|        <div class="cta-box">
   320|            <h2>Get Your Personalized Cancer Treatment Quote</h2>
   321|            <p>Connect with China's top oncology specialists and receive a detailed treatment plan with transparent pricing.</p>
   322|            <a href="../contact.html" class="cta-button">Request Free Consultation →</a>
   323|        </div>
   324|
   325|        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
   326|
   327|        <h3>Is the quality of cancer care in China comparable to Western countries?</h3>
   328|        <p>Yes. Top Chinese cancer hospitals are JCI accredited and many are ranked among the world's best. Chinese oncologists publish extensively in international journals and participate in global clinical trials.</p>
   329|
   330|        <h3>How long do I need to stay in China for treatment?</h3>
   331|        <p>Duration varies by treatment type: Surgery typically requires 2-3 weeks; chemotherapy cycles may span 3-6 months with periodic visits; radiation therapy usually requires 4-6 weeks of daily treatment.</p>
   332|
   333|        <h3>Will my insurance cover treatment in China?</h3>
   334|        <p>Many international insurance plans cover overseas treatment. We can provide all necessary documentation for insurance claims. Some patients also use medical tourism insurance.</p>
   335|
   336|        <h3>Is language a barrier?</h3>
   337|        <p>No. Major cancer hospitals have dedicated international departments with English-speaking staff. Medical translators are available for consultations and throughout your treatment.</p>
   338|
